{:ruleset :compustat
 :statement :income
 :taxonomy "us-gaap"
 :version "2026-10-15"
 :notes "Reclassification rules approximating Compustat income statement item
definitions, as an independent empirical approximation computed from public
SEC filings only. Developed and checked against a licensed Compustat annual extract
(18 large industrials; fitted on FY2010-2015, checked out-of-sample on
FY2016+): match rates within 1% are quoted per rule as as-reported ->
reclassified. Original line items are always preserved alongside the
reclassified ones. Residual gaps are footnote-level allocations and tags
Compustat keys from disclosures absent in the companyfacts API (e.g. partial
D&A splits between COGS and SG&A, R&D embedded in COGS, INDL-format
restatements of firms with finance arms, and expense lines carried only in
filer extension taxonomies - AMZN's Fulfillment and Technology & Content,
which Compustat folds into XSGA/XRD, are extension tags invisible here)."
 :aux {:cash-flow ["D&A" "Depreciation" "Amortization of Intangibles"]
       :concepts ["DepreciationDepletionAndAmortization"
                  "DepreciationAndAmortization"
                  "DepreciationAmortizationAndAccretionNet"
                  "ExplorationExpense"
                  "OperatingCostsAndExpenses"
                  "TaxesOther"
                  "CostOfPurchasedOilAndGas"
                  "OilAndGasRevenue"
                  "RevenueFromContractWithCustomerIncludingAssessedTax"]}
 :fsds
 {:markers
  [{:label "D&A Presented on Income Statement"
    :on-income-statement true
    :tags ["DepreciationDepletionAndAmortization"
           "DepreciationAndAmortization"
           "DepreciationAmortizationAndAccretionNet"
           "Depreciation"
           "DepreciationNonproduction"
           "OtherDepreciationAndAmortization"]}
   {:label "R&D Not Presented on Income Statement"
    :on-income-statement false
    :tags ["ResearchAndDevelopmentExpense"
           "ResearchAndDevelopmentExpenseExcludingAcquiredInProcessCost"
           "ResearchAndDevelopmentExpenseSoftwareExcludingAcquiredInProcessCost"]}]
  :extension-labels
  [["(?i)^fulfil?lment" "Fulfillment Expense"]
   ["(?i)^technologyand(content|infrastructure)" "Technology and Content Expense"]]}
 :rules
 [{:id :dp-components
   :target "DP (Compustat)"
   :compustat "DP"
   :formula [:+ "Depreciation" [:opt "Amortization of Intangibles"]]
   :guards [[:at-least [:+ "Depreciation" [:opt "Amortization of Intangibles"]]
             "DepreciationDepletionAndAmortization" 0.5]
            [:at-least [:+ "Depreciation" [:opt "Amortization of Intangibles"]]
             "DepreciationAndAmortization" 0.5]
            [:at-least [:+ "Depreciation" [:opt "Amortization of Intangibles"]]
             "DepreciationAmortizationAndAccretionNet" 0.5]]
   :notes "Compustat DP = property depreciation + intangible amortization. When a
filer tags Depreciation separately, the component sum beats the combined
cash-flow D&A tag, whose scope can exceed Compustat DP (AMZN's includes
capitalized-content amortization: 48.7B tagged vs 30.9B DP in 2023 =
Depreciation 30.2B + intangible amortization 0.7B exactly). Out-of-sample
FY2016+: DP 66% -> 76%, and COGS 43% -> 54% via the better operand, with
no in-sample cost. The guards reject a Depreciation tag that is a footnote
fragment - less than half of any combined D&A tag the filer reports (UPS
FY2019 tags Depreciation 212M against D&A 2.36B)."}
  {:id :dp-largest-tag
   :target "DP (Compustat)"
   :compustat "DP"
   :formula [:max "DepreciationDepletionAndAmortization" "DepreciationAndAmortization"
             "DepreciationAmortizationAndAccretionNet"]
   :notes "When no usable Depreciation component exists: the largest of the
combined D&A tags the filer reports. Filers often tag more than one, and the
smaller is typically a footnote subset (UPS FY2023-2025 tag
DepreciationDepletionAndAmortization 2.8-3.0B in a note and
DepreciationAndAmortization 3.4-3.7B on the cash flow statement, which
equals Compustat DP; AAPL FY2010-2014 likewise). The cost: AMZN FY2012-2013,
whose larger tag includes content amortization."}
  {:id :dp
   :target "DP (Compustat)"
   :compustat "DP"
   :formula [:= "D&A"]
   :notes "Fallback: the cash-flow statement's D&A line item, including the
standardized view's derived D&A."}
  {:id :cogs-oil-gas
   :target "COGS (Compustat)"
   :compustat "COGS"
   :formula [:+ "Cost of Revenue" "OperatingCostsAndExpenses" "TaxesOther"
             [:opt [:neg "Excise Taxes"]]]
   :guards [[:present "ExplorationExpense"]]
   :notes "Integrated oil presentation (an ExplorationExpense line identifies it):
Compustat COGS = purchased crude and products + operating expenses + taxes
other than on income, net of the excise taxes those taxes include in earlier
years. Exact for CVX FY2014-2025 (FY2023: 119196 + 24887 + 4220 = 148303M;
FY2014: 157496 - excise 8186 = 149310M). D&A and exploration are separate
lines and stay out."}
  {:id :cogs-oil-gas-purchased
   :target "COGS (Compustat)"
   :compustat "COGS"
   :formula [:+ "CostOfPurchasedOilAndGas" "OperatingCostsAndExpenses" "TaxesOther"
             [:opt [:neg "Excise Taxes"]]]
   :guards [[:present "ExplorationExpense"]]
   :notes "Same construction for filers tagging purchases as
CostOfPurchasedOilAndGas (outside the Cost of Revenue chain)."}
  {:id :cogs-da-presented
   :target "COGS (Compustat)"
   :compustat "COGS"
   :formula [:= "Cost of Revenue"]
   :guards [[:present "D&A Presented on Income Statement"]]
   :notes "FSDS placement guard: when the filer presents D&A as its own income
statement line, the reported cost-of-revenue line already excludes it and
stripping DP would double-count. The marker row is injected from FSDS pre.txt
(only when the FSDS cache is enabled), so this rule never fires otherwise."}
  {:id :cogs-ex-da
   :target "COGS (Compustat)"
   :compustat "COGS"
   :formula [:- "Cost of Revenue" "DP (Compustat)"]
   :guards [[:lt "DP (Compustat)" "Cost of Revenue"]]
   :notes "Compustat COGS excludes D&A. In the dominant filer pattern Compustat
removes the FULL DP from COGS, none from SG&A (IBM, INTC, KO, WMT, AAPL, CAT
all show a ~1.00 COGS fraction). 1% -> 57% in-sample. With the FSDS cache
enabled, the D&A-on-CF-only placement signal is what licenses this strip;
D&A-on-IS filers are caught by :cogs-da-presented above."}
  {:id :xsga-oil-gas
   :target "XSGA (Compustat)"
   :compustat "XSGA"
   :formula [:+ "SG&A Expense" "ExplorationExpense"]
   :notes "Integrated oil presentation: Compustat XSGA = SG&A + exploration
expense; R&D sits inside operating expenses and is not added (CVX FY2023:
4141 + 914 = 5055M exactly; 13 of 17 CVX years within 1%)."}
  {:id :xsga-rd-off-statement
   :target "XSGA (Compustat)"
   :compustat "XSGA"
   :formula [:= "SG&A Expense"]
   :guards [[:present "R&D Not Presented on Income Statement"]]
   :notes "FSDS placement guard: a filer that discloses R&D only in the notes
carries it inside another expense line already (SG&A or cost of sales), so
adding the tagged R&D amount would count it twice (PG, PEP: SG&A + R&D runs
5-10% above Compustat XSGA every year). The marker row comes from FSDS
pre.txt and needs the FSDS cache; without it the rule below adds R&D."}
  {:id :xsga-plus-rd
   :target "XSGA (Compustat)"
   :compustat "XSGA"
   :formula [:+ "SG&A Expense" [:opt "R&D Expense"]]
   :notes "Compustat XSGA folds R&D into SG&A (XRD stays broken out separately as
its own item). 20% -> 42%. Caveat: filers that embed R&D in COGS and tag the
notes value (e.g. HON) are over-added; not detectable from companyfacts."}
  {:id :xsga-components
   :target "XSGA (Compustat)"
   :compustat "XSGA"
   :formula [:+ "Selling and Marketing Expense" "General and Administrative Expense"
             [:opt "R&D Expense"]]
   :notes "Component fallback for filers with no combined SG&A tag (MSFT, ORCL,
CSCO tag S&M and G&A separately)."}
  {:id :xsga-opex-lines
   :target "XSGA (Compustat)"
   :compustat "XSGA"
   :formula [:+ "General and Administrative Expense" [:opt "Marketing Expense"]
             [:opt "Fulfillment Expense"] [:opt "Technology and Content Expense"]
             [:opt "R&D Expense"]]
   :notes "E-commerce presentation fallback (AMZN): no SG&A or S&M tag; the
operating expense lines besides cost of sales - fulfillment, marketing,
technology, G&A - all land in Compustat XSGA (empirically, the operating
expenses a filer reports alongside a COGS line resolve to XSGA). Fulfillment and
Technology & Content are extension tags supplied as FSDS operand rows when the
FSDS cache is enabled; without it this rule still fires but understates.
The other-operating line is excluded whichever way it is tagged
(OtherCostAndExpenseOperating or OtherOperatingIncomeExpenseNet):
empirically Compustat XSGA leaves it out - adding it overshoots and
subtracting it undershoots by the same amount (AMZN FY2018-2024)."}
  {:id :revt-incl-tax-ex-excise
   :target "Revenue (Compustat)"
   :compustat "REVT"
   :formula [:- "RevenueFromContractWithCustomerIncludingAssessedTax" "Excise Taxes"]
   :notes "Compustat REVT is net of excise taxes: a filer that tags its gross
revenue as IncludingAssessedTax and its excise taxes separately gets the
difference. Preferred over the Revenue chain, whose generic Revenues tag can
be a total that also includes equity-affiliate and other income (CVX
FY2016: 110215 - 6905 = 103310M exactly, where Revenues is 114472M)."}
  {:id :revt-oil-gas
   :target "Revenue (Compustat)"
   :compustat "REVT"
   :formula [:- "OilAndGasRevenue" [:opt "Excise Taxes"]]
   :guards [[:present "ExplorationExpense"]]
   :notes "Integrated oil presentation: sales and other operating revenues
(OilAndGasRevenue) net of excise, leaving out the income from equity
affiliates and other income that the filer's Revenues total includes. Exact
for CVX FY2009-2015 (FY2009: 167402 - 8109 = 159293M)."}
  {:id :revt-ex-excise-gp-tieout
   :target "Revenue (Compustat)"
   :compustat "REVT"
   :formula [:- "Revenue" "Excise Taxes"]
   :guards [[:concept-in "Gross Profit" #{"GrossProfit"}]
            [:ties [:- "Revenue" "Cost of Revenue" "Excise Taxes"] "Gross Profit" 0.005]]
   :notes "Compustat REVT is net of excise taxes. Arithmetic proof that the
tagged revenue still contains excise: the filer's reported GrossProfit ties
out (within 0.5%) to Revenue - Cost of Revenue - Excise Taxes. Catches filers
whose revenue tag claims to exclude assessed taxes while the value includes
them (MO FY2016-2019 tag RevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax
for net revenues that include excise: FY2016 25.744B - 7.765B - 6.407B =
reported GrossProfit 11.572B), which the concept-name guard below cannot
see. Needs a reported GrossProfit tag and a tagged excise line."}
  {:id :revt-ex-excise
   :target "Revenue (Compustat)"
   :compustat "REVT"
   :formula [:- "Revenue" "Excise Taxes"]
   :guards [[:concept-not-in "Revenue"
             #{"RevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax"}]]
   :notes "Compustat REVT is net of excise taxes. Applies only when the winning
revenue concept is not already net of assessed taxes and the filer tags an
excise-tax line. The guard trusts the concept name; the tie-out rule above
covers filers whose ExcludingAssessedTax revenue still includes excise when
they also report GrossProfit, but without a reported gross profit such
mis-tagged revenue goes un-netted. Excise lines tagged outside the Excise
Taxes chain (e.g. as a cost-of-revenue component) are not seen."}
  {:id :revt
   :target "Revenue (Compustat)"
   :compustat "REVT"
   :formula [:= "Revenue"]
   :notes "No excise netting applies: REVT is the Revenue line as tagged, so the
item exists for every filer, not only excise filers. 92% within 1% on the
13 industrials (first-reported values)."}
  {:id :gross-profit-net-revenue
   :target "Gross Profit (Compustat)"
   :compustat "REVT - COGS"
   :formula [:- "Revenue (Compustat)" "COGS (Compustat)"]
   :notes "Gross profit approximating Compustat's construction: REVT (excise-
netted where that applies) less COGS before D&A."}
  {:id :xopr
   :target "XOPR (Compustat)"
   :compustat "XOPR"
   :formula [:+ "COGS (Compustat)" "XSGA (Compustat)"]
   :notes "Total operating expenses excluding D&A; Compustat's XOPR = COGS + XSGA
identity. 43% within 1%."}
  {:id :special-items-combined-restructuring
   :target "Special Items (Compustat)"
   :compustat "SPI (operating portion)"
   :formula [:neg-sum "Restructuring Charges" "Goodwill Impairment"
             "Acquisition-Related Costs" "Litigation Settlement" "In-Process R&D"]
   :guards [[:concept-in "Restructuring Charges"
             #{"RestructuringCostsAndAssetImpairmentCharges"
               "RestructuringSettlementAndImpairmentProvisions"}]]
   :notes "Filers whose restructuring concept already includes asset
impairments: the separate Impairment Charges operand would double-count, so
it is dropped here (Goodwill Impairment stays - not inside the combined
tags). No filer on the validation sample triggers this today (A/B measured
identical, 2026-08-01), so the guard is pure protection."}
  {:id :special-items-aggregate-impairment
   :target "Special Items (Compustat)"
   :compustat "SPI (operating portion)"
   :formula [:neg-sum "Restructuring Charges" "Impairment Charges"
             "Acquisition-Related Costs" "Litigation Settlement" "In-Process R&D"]
   :guards [[:concept-in "Impairment Charges" #{"AssetImpairmentCharges"}]
            [:lte "Goodwill Impairment" "Impairment Charges"]]
   :notes "AssetImpairmentCharges is the aggregate asset write-down concept,
goodwill included; when the filer also tags GoodwillImpairmentLoss no larger
than it, the goodwill amount is taken to sit inside the aggregate and the
separate Goodwill Impairment operand is dropped. Confirmed on INTC FY2024:
AssetImpairmentCharges 3.631B is the 'asset impairment charges' line of its
restructuring-and-other-charges note, which the filing says includes 3.1B
of goodwill and acquired-intangible impairments (GoodwillImpairmentLoss
2.984B); adding both counted the goodwill twice. A goodwill amount larger
than the aggregate cannot be inside it and falls through to the rule
below."}
  {:id :special-items
   :target "Special Items (Compustat)"
   :compustat "SPI (operating portion)"
   :formula [:neg-sum "Restructuring Charges" "Impairment Charges" "Goodwill Impairment"
             "Acquisition-Related Costs" "Litigation Settlement" "In-Process R&D"]
   :notes "Compustat treats restructuring and impairment charges as special items
below the operating line. Sign follows Compustat: charges are negative. Only
the operating portion visible in XBRL tags is captured; non-operating special
items (divestiture gains etc.) are not. The combined-restructuring-tag
double-count case is handled by the guarded rule above."}
  {:id :cogs-total-costs
   :target "COGS (Compustat)"
   :compustat "COGS"
   :formula [:+ "Total Costs and Expenses" [:neg "DP (Compustat)"]
             [:opt "Special Items (Compustat)"]]
   :guards [[:absent "Cost of Revenue"] [:absent "SG&A Expense"]
            [:absent "Selling and Marketing Expense"]
            [:absent "General and Administrative Expense"]]
   :notes "Filers presenting expenses by nature (compensation, fuel, purchased
transportation, ...) with neither a cost-of-revenue nor an SG&A line:
Compustat puts all operating costs before D&A into COGS (XSGA stays empty,
COGS = XOPR). Built from the reported total less DP and less the special-
item charges inside it; placed after the special-items rules so the charge
is known. UPS: 15 of 17 years within 1%."}
  {:id :xopr-total-costs
   :target "XOPR (Compustat)"
   :compustat "XOPR"
   :formula [:+ "Total Costs and Expenses" [:neg "DP (Compustat)"]
             [:opt "Special Items (Compustat)"]]
   :guards [[:absent "Cost of Revenue"] [:absent "SG&A Expense"]
            [:absent "Selling and Marketing Expense"]
            [:absent "General and Administrative Expense"]]
   :notes "XOPR for the same presentation: equal to COGS, since there is no
XSGA to add."}
  {:id :oiadp
   :target "OIADP (Compustat)"
   :compustat "OIADP"
   :formula [:- "Operating Income" [:opt "Special Items (Compustat)"]
             [:opt "Gain (Loss) on Sale of Assets"]]
   :notes "Operating income after depreciation: OperatingIncomeLoss with special-
item charges added back (XBRL operating income includes them; Compustat
excludes them). 24% -> 41%. Nonrecurring asset-sale gains/losses (Compustat
GLP) are removed via subtraction because the XBRL tag is signed: a gain
(positive) is taken out of operating income, a loss (negative) is added back.
GLP is kept out of the Special Items row itself, whose :neg-sum operands are
positively-tagged charges. Untested hypothesis, not modeled: for industries
where asset sales are part of normal operations (e.g. oil, coal, transport)
recurring gains may belong in nonoperating income rather than special items.
A gain reported below the operating line would be over-removed, which
companyfacts cannot detect. On the validation sample removing the GLP
operand left OIADP unchanged (A/B 2026-08-01, consistent with the 2026-07-31
zero-marginal-effect check). No recurrence gate (e.g. treating gains seen in
three consecutive years as recurring) is implemented."}
  {:id :oiadp-bottom-up
   :target "OIADP (Compustat)"
   :compustat "OIADP"
   :formula [:- "Revenue (Compustat)" "XOPR (Compustat)" "DP (Compustat)"]
   :guards [[:absent "Operating Income"]
            [:ties [:+ "XOPR (Compustat)" "DP (Compustat)"] "Total Costs and Expenses" 0.02]]
   :notes "Filers that report no operating income line (e.g. CVX): REVT - XOPR -
DP, Compustat's own identity. Only when XOPR + DP reconciles to the filer's
reported total costs within 2% - the arithmetic evidence that the COGS and
XSGA reconstruction captured all operating costs. Without that tie-out
(IBM, HON, GE) the residual is several percent off and is not emitted."}
  {:id :oibdp
   :target "OIBDP (Compustat)"
   :compustat "OIBDP"
   :formula [:+ "OIADP (Compustat)" "DP (Compustat)"]
   :notes "Operating income before depreciation = OIADP + DP. Built top-down from
operating income (28% within 1%) rather than bottom-up as REVT - XOPR (19%);
as a consequence REVT - XOPR (Compustat) and OIBDP (Compustat) need not agree
exactly for firms with expense lines outside the COGS/XSGA reconstruction."}
  {:id :xrd-reported
   :target "XRD (Compustat)"
   :compustat "XRD"
   :formula [:= "R&D Expense"]
   :notes "Compustat XRD as a first-class reclassified item (supplementary and
non-additive: R&D is already folded into the XSGA reclassification)."}
  {:id :xrd-tech-content
   :target "XRD (Compustat)"
   :compustat "XRD"
   :formula [:= "Technology and Content Expense"]
   :notes "Filers with no R&D tag whose technology line Compustat keys as XRD:
AMZN's Technology and content / Technology and infrastructure extension tag
equals Compustat XRD exactly (verified on FY2025 vs the 2026Q1 FSDS). The
operand is an FSDS extension row - without the FSDS cache this rule cannot
fire."}]}
